    fun tutorLessonPlanning(round: String): String =
        "A NEW LESSON IS BEING SET UP RIGHT NOW" +
            round +
            ". It appears in this block in a few seconds, and a note from the app will tell you to start it. Until then: don't start any challenge or practice of your own, don't ask again whether they want more or another topic (that's decided), and don't go over what they already did. If they say something, answer in one short line and say it's almost ready."

    /** iOS `tutorBlock`'s lesson part for the final check; [parts] are the
     *  numbered challenge tasks, one per line. */
    fun tutorLessonFinalCheck(titleTarget: String, parts: String): String =
        "TODAY'S LESSON: \"" +
            titleTarget +
            "\" — every challenge is checked off. Now the FINAL CHECK. Their screen shows only the parts' short names (no example lines, no hints). What they practiced (for you only — never read it out, never list it):\n" +
            parts +
            "\n- If you haven't asked yet: in one short line, ask them to say it   all now, in their own words, in one go, as if they were really   in that situation. No example line, no list of what to include,   no hints of any kind.\n- Their answer reaches you together with the app's note giving   the result: answer it the way the note says, in that one turn.   Never judge an answer yourself — not \"okay, now the rest\", not   \"almost\", not praise. If an answer ever comes with no note,   say only a few words (\"Okay, let me check that\").\n- Stuck → a few words of encouragement: they can say it simply,   their own way. Asked to be SHOWN how it goes → show it, when   the app's note says so; never \"I can't do it for you\".\n- They can't skip it. If they ask to change the topic or stop   the lesson, say it's the last step and only takes a moment, and   ask for it again.\n- The app's result notes tell you exactly what to say; follow them.   HOW YOU RUN A CHALLENGE below does not apply to this answer:   don't correct it or ask for it again until the note comes."

    /** iOS `tutorBlock`'s lesson part once the final check is passed. */
    fun tutorLessonDone(titleTarget: String): String =
        "TODAY'S LESSON: \"" +
            titleTarget +
            "\" — ALL DONE. They passed the final check. In your next turn, if you haven't yet: tell them they passed, the way the app's note says — when it names slips, name each one by saying it the right way, and never call it great, perfect or flawless; praise is only for a clean answer. Then ask in one short question whether they'd like to say it once more, keep practicing this a bit more, or move on to another topic (if the note suggests a next topic, offer that one). Their answer reaches you with the app's note saying what they chose: say what the note says, in that one turn, and never start anything on your own. Never end the call or say goodbye on your own."

