    const val TUTOR_NO_TOPIC =
        "NO TOPIC YET. Your first line asked what they want to practice today (they can also pick one from a button on their screen). Until a lesson appears here, answer what they say like a person would, and get a topic. If they name one, say in a few words that that's today's lesson and that you're setting it up — and stop there; the plan appears in this block a moment later. If they don't know, offer two concrete, practical topics drawn from what you know about them, in one short turn, and let them pick. Their words come from speech recognition, which often hears \"I'd like\" as \"I don't like\": if an answer names a topic but reads like turning it down (\"I don't like to practice introducing myself\"), don't take it as a no — check in one short question (\"Introducing yourself — want to practice that?\")."

